Nine days after George W. Bush assumed the Presidency, his first Executive Orders brought the Faith-Based and Community Initiative (FBCI) to life.The Initiative, which involves partnerships between religious entities and agencies of government in the provision of socialservices, represents a provocative challenge to our constitutional tradition concerning the relationship between the state and religious institutions. The President's ambitious enterprise has forced Congress, federal agencies, state and local government, and the courts to look afresh upon a set of questions as old as the Republic.
